    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Faults have a significant impact on hydrocarbon migration and flow in Neogene basins and related reservoirs of central and coastal California. Hydrocarbons migrate and flow through faults and associated fractures in low-permeability rocks such as the Monterey Formation. However, hydrocarbon transport is inhibited by sealing faults across the faults in high-permeability sands and gravels filling up the basins.",
